#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1445 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note "THE PMDA-vs-FDA DISCRIMINATOR: the two 'Y' records differ only in VSTSTDTL, which IS in this rule's key set per the PMDA sheet row, so the tuples are distinct and nothing fires. Under the FDA twin's key set (which lacks --TSTDTL) this pair would fire. Also pins that the model-only VSTSTDTL column participates via the EC-36 textual prefix resolution."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset VS class=FINDINGS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col VSSEQ    type=Num
col VSTESTCD type=Char
col VSTSTDTL type=Char
col VSLOBXFL type=Char
---
S1 | VS | 001 | 1 | SYSBP | REST     | Y
S1 | VS | 001 | 2 | SYSBP | EXERCISE | Y
